    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm studying phonetics and i'm a bit confused. can you explain the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives? specifically the difference between /s/ and /z/ sounds in terms of what the vocal cords are doing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'd be happy to help clarify the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives for you. The main difference between /s/ (voiceless) and /z/ (voiced) lies in the interaction of the vocal cords. In /s/, the vocal cords are relaxed and not vibrating, accounting for the voiceless quality. In contrast, /z/ involves a vocal cord vibration, producing a voiced sound. When you say \"buzz\" or \"zip,\" the /z/ sound is more noticeable, while /s/ is softer.",
      "source": "target",
